# Running Python SDK tests

- Use the venv from [`docs/building-on-linux.md`](../../docs/building-on-linux.md):
  `source ~/dev/space-expansion-venv/bin/activate` (path there is
  `$SPEX_VENV_DIR`, default `~/dev/space-expansion-venv`). If it doesn't
  exist report user that since venv is not created, tests cannot run. Refer user
  to `docs/building-on-linux.md`.
- The SDK isn't installed as a package — export
  `PYTHONPATH=<repo>/python-sdk` before running tests.
- Run a specific test module directly, e.g.
  `python -m unittest expansion.unit_tests.procedures.test_navigation -v`.
  Don't `python -m unittest discover` over all of `expansion/unit_tests` —
  `expansion/unit_tests/types/` collides with the stdlib `types` module and
  breaks discovery; that failure is pre-existing and unrelated to your change.
